35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The records show that the same people have held the covered spots for years without review. Also, complaints about bikes leaning on each other were ignored because no one was held accountable. This lack of clarity creates hidden tension.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit sad to hear that, Misaki-san. I noticed that some of our neighbors have to move other bikes just to leave in the morning, and some poor bicycles are left out in the rain.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"The money side is even more boring than I thought. The ledger is basically empty, and the treasurer is spending hours on tiny cash collections. We're wasting time on pennies while the building gets no upgrades.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,The administrative burden is already significant. The treasurer spends three hours a month on minor collections; adding per-space billing would only increase that workload. We must avoid creating a system that exhausts whoever is in charge.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I knew it! The minutes prove the same flats have kept the covered spots for five years without any review! That's totally unfair! Plus, some daily riders are even willing to pay just to secure a spot!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, while the lack of review is unfair, we must be careful. If we suddenly strip people of spots they've had for years, it could create a cold atmosphere in the lobby. We need a transition that doesn't feel like a punishment.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki-san, you are so thoughtful. I worry that the morning rush is already a bit stressful for some. If we can make it easier to get out without shifting other bikes, everyone will feel much more relaxed.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, ""cold atmospheres"" don't pay for building repairs. If people are willing to pay for spots, as @Mio mentioned, why are we letting that money vanish? We should turn this into a revenue stream for the building.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, revenue is fine, but not at the cost of the treasurer's sanity. If we implement a complex payment system, we are just adding more hours of tedious paperwork to an already burdened role. We need a low-maintenance solution.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, I get that, but we can't just keep things the same because it's ""easy""! It's not fair to the people who've been left out for five years. We need a fresh start for everyone!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a fresh start is ideal, but we must avoid a situation where neighbors start avoiding each other. If we prioritize fairness too aggressively, we risk turning our lobby into a place of silence and resentment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio-san, I understand your heart, but perhaps we can find a way to be fair without being harsh. A gentle change might be easier for everyone to accept with a smile.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, smiles don't fix the budget. @George, if we set a flat, meaningful fee, it's not ""tedious paperwork""—it's an investment. Let's stop worrying about feelings and start thinking about the building's value.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, a flat fee still requires tracking, collecting, and reconciling. If the current system already takes three hours a month for ""pennies,"" adding more layers of billing will only lead to the same burnout we've seen before.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, I'm with you on the money part! If people are willing to pay, let's use it! But @George, maybe we can find a way to make it easy? We can't just let the same people win forever!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We have a conflict between fairness, budget, and administrative ease. However, we must not forget that we live here together. Let's look for an option that balances these needs without destroying our neighborly bonds.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Misaki-san. Let us remember that a bicycle is just a thing, but our kindness to one another is a treasure. I hope we can find a way that eases the morning rush for everyone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"Kindness is a treasure, sure, but a well-funded building is a luxury. Let's be pragmatic: we have a demand for spots and a budget that's practically nonexistent. It's time we stop being shy about charging for value.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"I must insist that we prioritize a system that is sustainable. If we choose a complex payment model, it will eventually collapse when the manager burns out. We need a solution that is simple to oversee and maintain.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm tired of the ""it's too hard"" excuse! We can't just ignore the fact that some people have been lucky for five years while others suffer. Let's find a way to be fair and practical at the same time!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
