60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B seems the safest for our relationships. By removing ""ownership"" of spots, we eliminate the resentment of favoritism and the tension of taking someone's place. It promotes a spirit of cooperation rather than competition.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B sounds very peaceful, Misaki-san. If we all share the space, we can help each other. However, I worry if the morning rush will still be a struggle with everyone crowding together.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B is just a recipe for chaos and more complaints. Why settle for ""cooperation"" when we can have actual funds? Option A is the only one that makes sense—it's fair, it's pragmatic, and it finally puts money in the account.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"@May, Option A is exactly what I fear. Adding monthly charges to the existing workload will only lead to the treasurer quitting. Option B is far more sustainable as it requires almost no ongoing administration.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, @George, Option B sounds okay, but it doesn't really solve the ""best spot"" problem—people will still fight over the easy ones! Option C is the most fair! Everyone gets a real chance every single year!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a lottery might seem fair on paper, but it creates a ""winner"" and a ""loser"" every year. That cycle of disappointment can lead to the very resentment and coldness I want us to avoid.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio-san, a lottery is exciting, but I worry about those who lose. It would be so sad to see a neighbor's face fall when they find out they have no spot for a whole year.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, @Shizue, you're both too worried about faces falling. Let's be honest: people are already unhappy. Option A solves the fairness issue by letting those who value the spot most pay for it, and it actually helps the building.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, you call it pragmatic, but it is a burden. Option A requires constant tracking and collection. Option B is the only choice that removes the administrative weight entirely, ensuring the system doesn't just collapse in a few months.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, but Option B is just a free-for-all! It doesn't stop the same people from hogging the best spots every day. Option C is a clean slate! It's a fresh start for everyone, and that's the only way to be truly fair!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a ""clean slate"" every year just resets the conflict. If we want to stop the cycle of complaints and hidden tension, we should move away from the idea of ""owning"" a spot entirely. Option B is the most harmonious.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki-san, you make a very good point. If we stop thinking about ""owning"" a spot, we can focus on being kind to one another. I hope the new racks make it easier to leave in the morning.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, @Shizue, you're prioritizing ""harmony"" over actual progress. Option B is just a fancy way of saying ""let's hope everyone behaves."" Option A is the only adult solution—it values the space and funds our building. Let's be bold!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"@May, being ""bold"" is useless if the system is abandoned because it's too tedious. Option A is a management nightmare. Option B is the only practical choice that doesn't rely on someone's unpaid labor to function.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, I like the money part, but @George is right about the work! But @Misaki, Option B is just a gamble every morning! Option C is the only way to guarantee a fair turn for everyone! I'm voting C!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May"",""George"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I still believe Option B is the best path. It removes the hierarchy of ""winners"" and ""losers"" and prevents the long-term resentment that comes with fixed spots. Let's choose harmony and simplicity over competition. I vote for B.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with Misaki-san. While I worry about the morning rush, I believe that by sharing the space, we can learn to be more considerate of one another. Let us choose kindness. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,You're all choosing the path of least resistance. We have a building that needs money and a system that needs a real value. I'm sticking to my guns. Let's be professional. I vote for A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,"I cannot support Option A due to the administrative burden, and Option C still requires annual management. Option B is the only sustainable choice that ensures the system won't collapse from burnout. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm the only one left! I really wanted a lottery to break the cycle of favoritism, but if everyone else is so sure about Option B, I'll go with the flow! I vote for B!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
